STRINGS:
1. length()
Returns the number of characters in a string.
Ex:String s="Java";
System.out.println(s.length());
output: 4

2. charAt()
Returns the character at a specified index.
Ex: String s="Java";
System.out.println(s.charAt(1));
output: a

3. toUpperCase()
Converts all characters into uppercase.
Ex: String s="Java";
System.out.println("s.toUpperCase());
output:JAVA

4. toLowerCase()
Converts all characters into lowercase.
Ex: String s="JAVA";
System.out.println("s.toLowerCase());
output:java

5. equals()
Compares two strings based on their content.
Ex: String a="Java";
String b="Java";
System.out.println(a.equals(b));
output: true

6. equalsignoreCase()
Compares Strings without considering uppercase or lowercase differences.
Ex:String a="JAVA";
String b="java";
System.out.println(a.equalsIgnoreCase(b));
output:true

7. contains()
Checks whether a string contains a particular sequence of characters.
Ex: String s="Java Programming";
System.out.println(s.contains("Java"));
output: true

8. substring()
Extracts a part of a string.
Ex: String s="Programming";
System.out.println(s.substring(0,4));
output: Prog

9. replace()
Replaces characters or character sequences.
Ex: String s="Java";
System.out.println(s.replace('a','o'));
output:Jovo

10. trim()
Removes leading and trailing spaces.
Ex: String s = "Hello";
System.out.println(s.trim());
output: Hello

